  "answer_core": "You should not grant Marcus 15% equity, a CTO title, and a board seat this week. Those are irreversible commitments, and you still don’t know whether the partnership reduces or concentrates risk.\n\nKeep the conversation direct and constructive: tell him there is a real path to major upside and leadership, but only after proof. Set a short, specific window to test whether he can deliver the core platform work, whether that work actually supports revenue, whether team continuity improves, whether knowledge transfers out of him rather than bottlenecks around him, and whether he shows the governance behavior you need. Make clear what successful completion of that window would unlock.\n\nThis avoids both premature commitments and vague delay. You are giving him a serious, evidence‑based path, not turning the decision into valuation math or instrument selection before you know what the partnership actually does to the company.",
